+### ADR-142, Amendment 9 (17 November 2026) — the v0.6.2 slice line: work cut by slice, gates as hooks and scripts, a computed board — PROPOSED
+
+**Context.** The owner's settings of 17 November 2026 and the slice line proposal of 16 November. The last cycle's
+faults were cut by layer and kept by promise: a heartbeat agents were asked to keep went stale; 251 carries crossed
+lanes; "done" was an agent's statement; rules were paragraphs that broke under pressure; the owner was the message
+bus. Built and shown red-then-green on `lane/slice-line-setup` (`process/lanes/v062/slice-line/README.md`).
+
+**Decision.** For v0.6.2, ADR-142's lanes give way to slices, and these decisions change:
+
+1. **Roles (decision 1).** One conductor (the owner's one session; writes no product code), scouts (read-only
+   subagents), one builder per slice in its own worktree on `lane/slice-<ID>`, and a verifier that never built the
+   slice. Builders and verifiers are separate `claude -p` sessions on the account `accounts.yaml` names, started by
+   `run_seat.py` with the guard loaded; permission mode `dontAsk` with each seat's tools pre-allowed.
+2. **Merging and pushing (decision 6).** `merge_slice.py` is the only writer to `main`, one branch at a time, and
+   only with: the slice's frozen acceptance test red before the slice and green on the merge result; today's full
+   gate green on the merge result (`stack_lease.sh offline merger -- make -k ci`, then the live files the change
+   reaches); a verifier's pass record for the branch's exact tip from a session that did not build it; no protected
+   path touched. It fast-forwards main to the tested merge commit, then `push_main.sh` pushes `main` to `origin`
+   only: never another remote, branch or tag, never a force, and never while a CI run on main is in progress (the
+   push waits, recorded, rather than cancel the run). Agents never push. `PUSH_LOG.md` gives way to
+   `~/.ospreyflow/slice-line/push.log`. The conductor's records reach main through the same script's records mode
+   (`process/lanes/v062/` only, never `dial.yaml` or `accounts.yaml`).
+3. **The heartbeat (decision 9)** gives way to `board.py`, computed from the backlog file on main, the branches, the
+   verifier's records and the test records; it is the only writer of the progress dashboard's `status.js`.
+4. **Rules that refuse.** The standing rules' enforceable parts are PreToolUse hooks run from a fixed place outside
+   every worktree (`~/.ospreyflow/slice-line/bin/`): the owner's files, never-staged files, pushing, a builder outside
+   its worktree, writes to main, credentials and the owner's address, the GOV.UK demo and airbyte, and the line
+   itself. A builder's Stop hook runs the slice's frozen checks and sends back the failures only.
+5. **The dial and the accounts** are the owner's files; neither is read by any gate. A started slice keeps its
+   setting, its accounts and its frozen acceptance and checks; only the owner changes them (`refreeze.py`).
+
+**What is not reopened.** Rule 14 (one agent per worktree, one holder of the dev stack), the lease and its stacks
+(decision 4), and every standing rule in `process/CLAUDE.md`.
+
+**Tests, named.** `OspreyFlow_Build/scripts/slice_line/tests/test_gates.py` (41 cases, through `tests/run.sh`) and
+`tests/plant_faults.py` (28 planted faults, each turning its test red).
+
+**Cost.** A merge waits for the full gate on the server (about the length of `make -k ci` there) and for main's
+own gate to be green: while main is red, every merge is refused. Shell commands are judged by their text, so the
+merge script's diff check, not the guard, is the backstop for a computed path.
